WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.133
Since the 1970s, there have 

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:11.845
been at least 18 gangs within the Los
 Angeles County Sheriff's Department,

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:17.350
and they continue to brutalize
 and even murder community members today.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:25.275
My name is Cerise Castle
 and I am a journalist.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.528
In the summer of 2020, 

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:33.199
I was working for a local radio station
 here in Los Angeles,

00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:38.913
and I was out covering the George Floyd

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:43.585
rallies that were happening
 across the country across the world.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.006
I was shooting photos
 of people protesting,

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:54.387
and while I was doing that two cars
 with police officers on them

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:58.558
in riot gear rolled into the area
 where people had gathered

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:03.396
and they shot people
 with less lethal munitions.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.983
And although I identified myself as press,

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:13.114
I was shot and the resulting injuries
 landed me in the hospital.

00:01:14.532 --> 00:01:18.286
A few days after that happened,
 the Los Angeles Sheriff's Department

00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:21.623
killed a teenager 

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:25.627
who was working at his job
 in the Compton area.

00:01:26.294 --> 00:01:29.339
Very quickly after this
 young man was killed.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:33.635
His name is Andrés Guardado,
 it was reported that his killing

00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:37.555
may have been part of a gang initiation,
 and there are some new allegations against

00:01:37.555 --> 00:01:40.934
the deputy involved in Guardado's case
 who did not fire his weapon.

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:44.104
Civil rights attorneys accused Christopher
 Hernandez of being part

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:47.065
of what some call
 a sheriff's department clique or gang.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:52.028
While I was bedridden,
 I started researching

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:56.991
the history of the gangs in the Los
 Angeles County Sheriff's Department,

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:03.123
and I found out that this dates back
 at least 50 years.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.960
I spent six months

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.713
researching deputy gangs

00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:13.800
within the Los Angeles County
 Sheriff's Department.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:19.639
Conservatively, I estimate I read about
 100,000 pages of legal filings.

00:02:20.265 --> 00:02:23.810
And what I came away with
 was a 15 part series

00:02:24.352 --> 00:02:27.480
detailing 18 gangs that I was able

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.692
to confirm the existence
 of within the department.

00:02:31.276 --> 00:02:35.446
There are the Little Devil's posse,
 the Wayside Whities, the 2000

00:02:35.446 --> 00:02:39.659
Boys, the 3000 Boys, the Jump Out
 Boys, the Bandidos, the Executioners,

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.872
the Spartans, the Cowboys,
 the Rattlesnakes and the Tasmanian Devils.

00:02:44.539 --> 00:02:48.710
They have killed 19 people,
 all of whom were men of color,

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:52.255
several of whom were in a mental health
 crisis when they were killed.

00:02:54.382 --> 00:02:59.387
Government from the county level,
 the state level, and the federal level

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:03.641
has known about this issue
 since the early 1990s,

00:03:04.225 --> 00:03:08.271
and no significant action, policy change

00:03:08.563 --> 00:03:11.983
has been brought forth. 

00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:18.573
So let's do a quick run
 through of the gangs of the Los

00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:21.576
Angeles Sheriff's Department,
 all of them have stuff in common.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:27.123
You usually have official gang tattoos,
 a hand signal and a way to join, usually

00:03:27.123 --> 00:03:31.794
by shooting or killing a civilian or doing
 something like falsifying paperwork.

00:03:32.253 --> 00:03:35.256
These are just a few of the gangs
 operating within the L.A.

00:03:35.256 --> 00:03:37.050
Sheriff's Department. 

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.551
The Wayside Whities. 

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:42.847
The Wayside Whities was a gang of white
 deputies at the Pitches Detention Center

00:03:42.847 --> 00:03:43.681
in northern L.A. 

00:03:43.681 --> 00:03:46.684
County in the 1980s and 1990s.

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:51.648
Their sign was having their middle
 fingers crossed to create a "W" for White.

00:03:51.648 --> 00:03:53.691
The Lynwood Vikings. 

00:03:53.691 --> 00:03:56.402
The Vikings were a gang based
 out of the Lynwood station.

00:03:56.694 --> 00:03:59.530
Their tattoo was of a Viking
 and their hand sign was

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.450
an "L" made with the thumb
 and index finger for Lynwood.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:06.454
And they were one of the most powerful
 and most violent gangs.

00:04:06.663 --> 00:04:09.123
A lot of their members
 became leaders in the department.

00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:11.834
The 3000 Boys. the 

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:15.463
3000 Boys were based out of the men's
 central jail in downtown L.A.

00:04:15.964 --> 00:04:19.884
The 3000 boys are particularly violent
 because that's where the department would

00:04:19.884 --> 00:04:23.346
transfer deputies convicted of crimes
 to keep them away from the public.

00:04:24.514 --> 00:04:26.557
The Jump Out Boys. the Jump Out boys

00:04:26.557 --> 00:04:29.936
operated across the county
 in the Operation Safe Streets unit.

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:34.232
Their tattoo was of a skeleton
 with glowing red eyes holding a revolver

00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:38.528
and the dead man's hand, a popular poker
 holding among law enforcement officers.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.947
They kept their manifesto in a notebook.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.827
The Regulators. Out of the Century
 Station, you have the regulators

00:04:45.827 --> 00:04:49.289
who allegedly have many members
 working in department leadership.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.500
The Executioners. 

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.461
At the Compton Station,
 you have the Executioners.

00:04:55.586 --> 00:04:59.966
Their tattoo is of a skeleton with a Nazi
 helmet holding an assault rifle.

00:05:00.216 --> 00:05:03.177
Black people and women are
 not allowed to join the gang.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:08.016
The Bandidos. The Bandidos operate
 mainly out of the East L.A.

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:11.853
station, and their tattoo is of a skeleton
 wearing a sombrero

00:05:11.853 --> 00:05:14.397
with a smoking revolver
 and a sheriff's badge.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:19.027
They have a culture of working backwards,
 arresting or shooting civilians

00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:23.489
